  "text": {
    "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
    "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-c26bb7a766@example.invalid",
    "text": "<p>Stryker has announced the installation of its 1,000th Mako System, a significant milestone for Mako SmartRobotics™.</p>\n<p>There are now more than 1,000 Mako Systems installed across 28 countries and in every state in the contiguous U.S. Introduced in 2006, Mako SmartRobotics™ now has over 14 years of clinical use, with over 350,000 robotic-arm-assisted surgery cases performed worldwide. Mako SmartRobotics™ combines three key components — 3D CT-based planning, AccuStop™ haptic technology and insightful data analytics* — into one platform, which has shown better outcomes for total hip, total knee and partial knee patients.<sup>1,2,3</sup></p>\n<p>“The installation of the 1,000th Mako is a milestone we are proud of, especially since the full launch of our Total Knee application just happened in 2016,” said Spencer Stiles, Stryker’s group president of Orthopaedics &amp; Spine. “Robotics in orthopaedics is here to stay, and at Stryker we are committed to further advancing this technology.”</p>\n",
    "jcr:lastModified": "Mon Sep 14 2020 17:11:46 GMT+0000",
    "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
    "textIsRich": "true"
  },
  "disclaimer": {
    "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
    "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-c26bb7a766@example.invalid",
    "disclaimer-type": "text",
    "disclaimer": "<p>References</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Illgen RL, Bukowski BR, Abiola R, et al. Robotic-assisted total hip arthroplasty: outcomes at minimum two year follow up. Surg Technol Int. 2017;30:365-372.</li>\r\n<li>Kayani B, Konan S, Tahmassebi J, Pietrzak JRT, Haddad FS. Robotic-arm assisted total knee arthroplasty is associated with improved early functional recovery and reduced time to hospital discharge compared with conventional jig-based total knee arthroplasty: a prospective cohort study. Bone Joint J. 2018;100-B(7):930-937. doi:10.1302/0301-620X.100B7.BJJ-2017-1449.R1</li>\r\n<li>Kleeblad LJ, Borus T, Coon TM, Dounchis J, Nguyen JT, Pearle AD. Midterm survivorship and patient satisfaction of robotic-arm assisted medial unicompartmental knee arthroplasty: a multicenter study. J Arthroplasty. 2018;33(6):1719-1726. doi:10.1016/j.arth.2018.01.0364</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<div>*Access to the data analytics offering requires execution of a separate agreement.</div>\r\n",
